== mini-troff sample.1
     SAMPLE(1)                                               SAMPLE(1)

     NAME
          sample, example - a page to try the macros of man(6) on

     SYNOPSIS
          sample [ -cds ] [ -o file ] [ name ... ]

     DESCRIPTION
          Sample does nothing: it is a page written to be typeset.
          Its first paragraph is long enough to be put on several
          lines, so that one sees where a line is ended when the next
          word does not fit.  A sentence ends here.  Not after e.g.
          this one, nor after a.out in the font of what is typed; it
          does after one.  A word with a hyphen may be cut after it,
          as in a twenty-seven-letter right-to-left never-ending word;
          not an option's, as
          -long-option-name-that-is-not-to-be-cut-anywhere-in-its-letters,
          and not a minus: -5.

          The options are:

          -c   Complement the set.  A tag shorter than its width has
               its text on its line.

          -d   Delete.

          -o file
               The tag is wider than five letters: its text starts
               below.

          -s          Squeeze, with a width said.

          -t          The width stays.
          -u
          -v          Two tags, one text, closed up.

          A paragraph, then one further right:

               Indented, with no tag.

          •  With a bullet.

             Inside a relative indent, `quoted' and `typed', the fonts
             in turn: troff(1), [-x] and SMALL .

          Back at the margin.

        A subsection
          A hanging paragraph has its first line at the margin and the
               others to its right, which shows only when it is long
               enough to have others.

          Lines that are not filled:

               int  n;   /* a tab, then another */
               char *name;
                    for(i = 0; i < n; i++)
                         print("%d\n", i);

          With stops of its own (.ta):
          name      size  what
          tr        12    translate

          A line moved by hand,
          a break,


          and two lines' space.
              One line further right, and the rest of this paragraph
          back where it was, as long as it takes to see it.
             The margin moved,
          and back.
                                    centered

     EXAMPLES
          A character by its name: -, •, →, 2×3; a backslash: \;
          italic, typed and smaller.

     SEE ALSO
          troff(1), man(6)
